# Style Rule: No Em-Dashes in Writing

- **No Em-Dashes:** Do not use literal em-dashes (`—`) or LaTeX triple-hyphen em-dashes (`---`) in any LaTeX documents or markdown files in this repository.
- **Alternative Punctuation:** Use colons, semicolons, parenthetical commas, or en-dashes (`--`) with spaces to represent pauses or parenthetical explanations, as they provide cleaner academic typesetting and avoid formatting issues.
- **Table Cells Exception:** Standard triple-hyphens `---` are permitted exclusively for indicating empty cells in LaTeX tables.
